  "schema_version": 1,
  "statement": "The public recipe was derived from the measured engineering recipe by identifier renames only (file names and string literals) plus re-pinning the two overlay-file hashes and the loader hook's after-hash that those renames change; that was the complete delta through v1.0.0, with no control flow, contract hash, transform seam, serving argument, or environment value changed. v1.0.1 adds one deliberate behavioral delta on top: the kpool transform target now applies the upstream launcher's GB10 persistent_topk disable (after-hash f48c5f93cb3c7d1b1238381761b65c142a1c032023dcef8e449a02f651fb0530 to 00e32052b781723500987a463814116634c4d00b3b61066915f8cc70780c931e), the exact file every measured arm executed. changed_lines is the unified-diff count of added plus deleted lines between the measured file and the public file. Measured-file hashes are listed so a reviewer holding the private bundle can confirm the mapping. v1.1.0 adds the Cadence layer: the six measured module files ship byte-for-byte (their measured and public hashes are identical by construction, taken from the measured bundle's module-hashes.json), config/cadence-contract.json, scripts/install_b45_modules.py, and scripts/long_context_witness.py are new public files with no measured-side counterpart (measured_sha256 and changed_lines are null rather than fabricated), and scripts/fleetctl.py plus scripts/container_entry.sh gain Cadence wiring on top of the historical rename-only delta (the changed_lines value keeps its v1.0.x meaning and is scoped explicitly by changed_lines_scope). tools/test_v11_offline.py is a public-only offline test tool with no measured-side counterpart and is therefore not a derivation row."
